  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "At the moment, making a player locally disappear from view for you requires messing with VRC Stations in a way that they were not really intended to be messed with.\nThere's a few good reasons why a Udon toggle for being able to make a player totally disappear would be a good idea:\n1. In game worlds, allow for 1 player sections, like cutscenes or tutorials.\n2. In private events, allow for vetting of a guest before they show up to anyone outside of a whitelist.\n3. In large maps, allow for area load/unload within the high-precision space near origin without seeing another player walking around on a different bit of the map.\n4. Performance - allowing a large number of people in a map but allowing players to limit the load somewhat if they have a weaker PC.\nNote that much of this is already possible with hacky implementations using stations. A visibility toggle just makes this easier.",
